{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1020593-creating-a-stage-magician-character","id":1020593,"title":"Creating a Stage Magician Character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-21T13:16:06-08:00","id":1020593,"title":"Creating a Stage Magician Character","content":"When creating a stage magician character, what sort of Traits would be necessary? Here's what I've come up with so far:<br /> <br /> Attributes: Mid- to High-Level ratings in Dexterity, Wits, and Presence and/or Manipulation would be essential, and Stamina would help with a number of Escapist tricks, namely the ones happening underwater.<br /> <br /> Skills: Larceny is a must for sleight-of-hand; Crafts for the use and possible construction of props; and Stealth for the old &quot;Now You See Me&quot; schtick. Subterfuge and Persuasion.can help with priming the audience.<br /> <br /> Merits: The usual set of Professional Merits (Professional Training, Area of Expertise, Interdisciplinary Specialty, <i>et al</i>), plus any for your particular act (Sleight of Hand, Double Jointed, etc.)<br /> <br /> Anyone have any additional suggestions? Or perhaps any ideas on how to better use the Skills I've mentioned?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:08:26-08:00","id":1020637,"title":"","content":"Maybe <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/933264-2e-illusionists-of-truth-%E2%80%93-magicians-legacy\">my Legacy for stage magic mages</a> will help you a bit on those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:14:22-08:00","id":1020642,"title":"","content":"I think you have covered the particulars quite thoroughly in your opening post. Take Larceny, Wits, and Dexterity to 3 dots, 2-3 dots in Stealth, Expression and Subterfuge, a specialty in Stage Tricks for Larceny with Area of Expertise, and the Sleight of Hand merit are pretty good minimums for a starting character with no experience points put in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T17:03:27-08:00","id":1020713,"title":"","content":"Yup, sounds like everything a mortal stage magician would need.<br /> <br /> Unless we're talking about supernaturals who are for some reason doing stage magic. Upon which the options get much wider and much more... interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:57:17-08:00","id":1020882,"title":"","content":"Empathy for cold reading audience members.<br /> <br /> Composure to avoid stage fright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf","user":"vernuf","date":". 12-22-2016, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf","name":"vernuf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:11:37-08:00","id":1020937,"title":"","content":"It would be appropriate to have dots in Expression, as stage magic is a performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T11:45:16-08:00","id":1020963,"title":"","content":"I'd take Omnidisciplinary Specialty: Stage Magic, so your character could apply their specialty bonus to ll roles that were in some way relevant. I'd also take a dot of Occult, to better window dress the stage magic being done (and perhaps recognise actual magic as well). It'd be great if you were making a character like Harry Houdini - he wasn't just an escape artist, but someone who debunked the supernatural conmen he found simply so he could find ACTUAL supernatural occurrences. He was big on trying to find if an afterlife existed, particularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T18:41:42-08:00","id":1022571,"title":"","content":"I think you've got the skill and attribute side covered, so I'll suggest a bit of supernatural influence instead. Mekhet and Nosferatu make great magicians because of their clan disciplines; both clans have obfuscate, which at higher levels can create illusions on objects. The Mekhet have Auspex which can be used for a mentalist kind of performance, and the Nosferatu have Nightmare which has illusion powers at level one. I can't offer much advice on other splats though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T22:36:53-08:00","id":1022623,"title":"","content":"As linked Legacy for Mage few posts above - best Stage Magicians Awakaned will be Mastigos and Acanthus. First ones even got signature character in 1E - Arctos from corebook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:33:22-08:00","id":1023263,"title":"","content":"Obrimos could be awesome stage magicians as well, the ability to bend light, but Mates have a key flaw as stage magicians, sleepers. <br /> <br /> Changelings are much better stage magicians, in 2e contractions of vainglory, contract of Air and Darkness, contract of hidden reality, contract of animate animation, contract of chystalis, and contract of elements. Really Vainglory + Air &amp; Darkness are enough by themselves, especially with Dropping the Mask and Embracing the Wyrd template abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:02:45-08:00","id":1023280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1020593-creating-a-stage-magician-character?p=1023263#post1023263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obrimos could be awesome stage magicians as well, the ability to bend light, but Mates have a key flaw as stage magicians, sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/933264-2e-illusionists-of-truth-%E2%80%93-magicians-legacy\">Legacy based entierly on Stage Magicians</a> - with Attainments, there is no Paradox or Dissonance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:35:02-08:00","id":1023315,"title":"","content":"While I like the idea of Stage magician mages, the concept of Changelings fits somehow even better, at least to me.<br /> Fairest would probably be the best, though I can totally see a Wizened or Darkling stage magician (or at least, part of the crew/motley). Especially for a Victorian setting, this would be cool.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T20:34:38-08:00","id":1023562,"title":"","content":"I actually had a notion for an escape artist Promethean once, inspired by Scott Free/Mister Miracle. High Dexterity, Stamina, Wits and Composure, skill dots in Crafts, Larceny, Athletics, Stealth, Subterfuge and Expression (plus a few others scattered about... my concept was that he was brought to life in a prison). Sleight of Hand and Double Jointed are obvious enough for Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:52:42-08:00","id":1023934,"title":"","content":"Over on the Beast forum, I created a stage magician character (with a Horror that was basically an evil rabbit) for a game. I can post his sheet and backstory here, if there is any interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T15:32:02-08:00","id":1023968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1020593-creating-a-stage-magician-character?p=1023934#post1023934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over on the Beast forum, I created a stage magician character (with a Horror that was basically an evil rabbit) for a game. I can post his sheet and backstory here, if there is any interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be quite interested. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T20:01:44-08:00","id":1024073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1020593-creating-a-stage-magician-character?p=1023968#post1023968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be quite interested. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, here is Nathaniel Hargrove, aka, Mordecai the Mysterious. First, his <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_AXRfImh-kVM1dhVi1zVkdQY0k/view\" target=\"_blank\">character sheet</a>. I also promised his <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_AXRfImh-kVSlIwOG1rRDNpSG8/view\" target=\"_blank\">backstory</a>. And just for good measure, here's the answers to the <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_AXRfImh-kVblA2YnZvbWg1TVU/view\" target=\"_blank\">followup questions</a> that the ST asked. I've gotten really attached to the character since creating him. He's shown up as an NPC at this point, and my wife has even said that she'd like to run a game for him at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T01:48:15-08:00","id":1024155,"title":"","content":"For some reason, he reminds Me Of